{"id": "section-body-04740", "title": ": Malaria chemoprophylaxis in sickle cell disease", "chapterId": "chapter-five", "tocLevel": 4, "tocPath": ["APPROACH TO PATIENTS WITH EMERGENCY CONDITIONS", "MALARIA", "Symptomatic Malaria Case", ": Malaria chemoprophylaxis in sickle cell disease"], "blocks": [{"id": "body-04740", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": ": Malaria chemoprophylaxis in sickle cell disease", "runs": [{"text": ":"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Malaria"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chemoprophylaxis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sickle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cell"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}], "level": 4, "list": {"level": 2, "numberingId": "1748"}}, {"id": "body-04741", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Sickle cell disease (SCD) is an inherited condition where the sickle cell gene responsible for the production of abnormal haemoglobin S is inherited from both parents.", "runs": [{"text": "Sickle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cell"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "disease"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(SCD)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "an"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "inherited"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "condition"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "where"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "sickle"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "cell"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "gene"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "responsible"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "for"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "the"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "production"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "abnormal haemoglobin S is inherited from both parents."}]}, {"id": "body-04742", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "In areas where malaria is common, SCD patients have low risk or malaria infection. However, when they do get malaria, it is associated with high risk of morbidity and mortality.", "runs": [{"text": "In areas where malaria is common, SCD patients have low risk or malaria infection. However, when they do get malaria, it"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is associated with high risk of morbidity and mortality."}]}, {"id": "body-04744", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "It is recommended to give routine malaria prevention medicines (chemoprophylaxis) to individuals with SCD in areas where malaria is endemic. This helps to reduce SCD crises and all other related complications.", "runs": [{"text": "It is recommended to give routine malaria prevention medicines (chemoprophylaxis) to individuals with SCD in areas where malaria is endemic. This helps to reduce SCD crises and all other related complications."}]}, {"id": "body-04745", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "The recommended chemoprophylaxis in Tanzania is:", "runs": [{"text": "The"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "recommended"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "chemoprophylaxis"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "in"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "Tanzania"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "is:"}]}, {"id": "body-04746", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: atovaquone + proguanil: daily administration according to body weight", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "atovaquone"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "+"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "proguanil:"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "daily"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "administration"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "according"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weight"}]}, {"id": "body-04747", "type": "paragraph", "style": "Heading3", "text": "OR", "runs": [{"text": "OR"}], "level": 3, "conjunction": true}, {"id": "body-04748", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "C: dihydroartemisinin + piperaquine (FDC) (PO): monthly administration according to body weight", "runs": [{"text": "C:", "bold": true}, {"text": " ", "bold": true}, {"text": "dihydroartemisinin"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "+"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "piperaquine"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(FDC)"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "(PO):"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "monthly"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "administration"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "according"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "body"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "weight"}]}, {"id": "body-04750", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Due to available safe and effective pharmacological action every SCD patient who require protection must receive a suitable chemoprevention treatment.", "runs": [{"text": "Due"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "to"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "available"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "safe"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "and"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "effective"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "pharmacological"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "action"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "every"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "SCD"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "patient"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "who"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "require"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "protection"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "must"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "receive"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "a"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "suitable chemoprevention treatment."}]}, {"id": "body-04752", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "text": "Management of fever", "runs": [{"text": "Management"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "of"}, {"text": " "}, {"text": "fever"}], "level": 4}, {"id": "body-04753", "type": "paragraph", "style": "BodyText", "text": "Patients with high fever (38.50C and above) should be given appropriate dose of anti-pyretic medicine like paracetamol or acetylsalicylic acid(aspirin) 6-8hourly (maximum 4doses in 24hours) until symptoms resolve, usually after 2-3days.", "runs": [{"text": "Patients with high fever (38.50C and above) should be given appropriate dose of anti-pyretic medicine like paracetamol or acetylsalicylic acid(aspirin) 6-8hourly (maximum 4doses in 24hours) until symptoms resolve, usually after 2-3days."}]}, {"id": "body-04755", "type": "heading", "style": "Heading4", "tex